      {
        "title": "Classifying Cell Populations by Radiosensitivity",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "In 1968, Rubin and Casarett grouped mammalian cell populations into five categories based on radiosensitivity, using cell death as the endpoint. Increasing radioresistance runs: "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "VIM \u2192 DIM \u2192 multipotential connective tissue cells \u2192 RPM \u2192 FPM",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "VIM and DIM Cells",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
