                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "An important exception:",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " the mature lymphocyte is classified as an RPM cell (which should be relatively radioresistant), but it's actually very radiosensitive \u2014 a well-known exception to the Law of Bergoni\u00e9 and Tribondeau."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page3_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Which classified cell type is a notable exception to the general radiosensitivity pattern predicted by its category?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "The mature lymphocyte",
              "The Type A spermatogonium"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The mature lymphocyte is classified as RPM (normally radioresistant), but is actually highly radiosensitive \u2014 a well-known exception."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Applying This to Tissues and Organs",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Every tissue and organ contains two compartments: "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "parenchyma",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " (the functional cells characteristic of that tissue \u2014 VIM, DIM, RPM, or FPM cells) and "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "stroma",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " (supporting connective tissue and vasculature, generally intermediate in radiosensitivity)."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "The radiosensitivity of a tissue or organ as a whole is determined by its "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "most sensitive",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "italic"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " parenchymal cell type. The testes and bone marrow are highly radiosensitive because their parenchyma includes VIM stem cells. Tissues containing only RPM or FPM parenchymal cells \u2014 like liver, muscle, brain, and spinal cord \u2014 are comparatively radioresistant."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "In radioresistant organs, damage often occurs indirectly: stromal (vascular) cells are damaged at lower doses than the parenchymal cells, reducing blood flow and oxygen/nutrient supply, which secondarily damages the parenchyma."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Wrap-Up",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "You've covered the five-category cell population classification (VIM, DIM, connective tissue, RPM, FPM), the mature lymphocyte exception, and how a tissue's overall radiosensitivity traces back to its most sensitive parenchymal cell type."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "This directly extends the Law of Bergoni\u00e9 and Tribondeau from the Cell Sensitivity lesson into a practical classification system you can apply to real tissues and organs."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
